Subject: Merge a version that the version loop completed

Merge a stack version with an equivalent version before it, as soon as the version loop completes
the work of that version.

The copy of the runtime of the tree-sitter-cpp fork has this repair. The fork commit is
50fb3cd.

The version loop of one parse step gives each version its own head, also
where two versions shift the same token into the same state. Only the
condense step at the end of the loop merges them. The list then holds
more versions than the mid-step limit of ts_parser__reduce at
lib/src/parser.c:1051. That limit removes a reduction by the index of
its version, and the tree depends on the state numbers of the parse
table. No ERROR node marks the result, and each grammar change that
moves the state count moves the reading.

In the C++ grammar of the fork, a template argument gives the type
reading the dynamic precedence 3 and the expression reading 1. [temp.arg]
p2 asks for the type reading, and GCC and Clang each read a type-id
first. For `namespace N::M { A::B<T1<...<I::J, I::K>>> g {}; }` the
limit removed the version of the type reading before a dynamic
precedence compared the two. The last argument got the expression
reading from 7 levels. From 14 levels the whole declaration became an
expression statement: a chain of comparisons with `<` and `>`, and a
compound literal `g {}` at the end.

At the 7-level form, the version list reached 55 heads, and 24 of them
had the same state at the same position. The condense step at the end of
the same parse step took 55 heads to 2. The overflow was made of
versions that a merge removes, and the budget of the mid-step limit went
to them.

The patch merges each version as soon as the loop completes its work,
and only where the list is longer than MAX_VERSION_COUNT. The mid-step
limit removed 14 reductions of the 7-level form before the patch and
none after it. For the 8-level form the count goes from 144 to 0. The
peak version count goes from 55 to 33 and from 53 to 43.

A merge removes no reading, because stack_node_add_link keeps the two
readings as two links of one node. A measurement counts 5 links that the
merge adds to one node, and zero links that the MAX_LINK_COUNT limit
removes.

A MERGE ONLY. DO NOT ADD A REMOVAL HERE. The first form of this patch
also removed a version that ts_parser__compare_versions makes
unnecessary, in the same way as the condense step. A fuzz run of
1,784,374 changes of 4,813 C++ files refuted it with two timeouts. A
mid-step removal is not the same operation as the condense step, for two
reasons. A version that the loop has no work for yet can get a lower
error cost later. And a removal takes the paused versions, which the
condense step resumes to start the recovery of an error. A C++ file of
85 KB with a string that has no end then went from 2.21 s to 28.53 s,
and a second file went from 0.02 s to 15.99 s. With the merge alone, the
first file parses in 1.99 s, which is faster than before the patch.

The removal gave a deeper repair: the type reading of the example held
to 18 levels with it, and to 10 levels without it. That depth is not
worth the error recovery.

On the corpus of 329,387 C++ files, the files with a parse error stay at
14,263, and the bytes in ERROR nodes stay at 6,693,662. Two files get a
different tree, and each of the two changes reads a template argument as
a type-id, which is the rule of [temp.arg] p2. No compiler test file of
the 7,646 gets a different tree. `xtask fuzz` finds no failure in
1,784,374 changes of 4,813 inputs. The parse time of the 12 slowest
corpus files, as the minimum of three runs, goes from 14.736 s to
14.758 s.

Risk for upstream: medium. The patch changes the version list inside a parse step, so it changes
which versions the condense step sees. It adds one O(n) scan for each version, and only where the
list is longer than MAX_VERSION_COUNT.

The patch applies to the upstream tag v0.27.0, after the patches with a smaller number. The
series compiles with `-Wall -Wextra` and no warning.

The comments hold the marker "(tree-sitter-cpp fork)". Remove the marker before you send the
patch upstream.

--- ts/lib/src/parser.c	2026-09-16 00:17:02.507445390 +0200
+++ ts-new/lib/src/parser.c	2026-09-16 00:35:42.690422183 +0200
@@ -2100,6 +2100,31 @@
   }
 }
 
+// Merge the version `version` with a version before it. Return true if the merge removed `version`,
+// and the caller subtracts one from its index.
+//
+// The version loop of one parse step gives each version its own head, also where two versions shift
+// the same token into the same state. Only the condense step at the end of the loop merges them.
+// The list then holds more versions than the mid-step limit of `ts_parser__reduce`, and that limit
+// drops a reduction by the index of its version. The reading of a deep template argument list then
+// depends on the state numbers of the parse table, and not on the dynamic precedences of the
+// grammar.
+//
+// The caller calls this function for each version that completes its turn. The function removes no
+// reading, because a merge keeps the two readings as two links of one node. It removes no version
+// that a comparison makes unnecessary, although the condense step removes such a version. A version
+// that has no turn yet can still get a lower error cost, and a removal before the condense step also
+// takes the candidates of the recovery of an error.
+static bool ts_parser__merge_finished_version(TSParser *self, StackVersion version) {
+  for (StackVersion j = 0; j < version; j++) {
+    if (ts_stack_merge(self->stack, j, version)) {
+      LOG("merge_finished_version version:%u into:%u", version, j);
+      return true;
+    }
+  }
+  return false;
+}
+
 static unsigned ts_parser__condense_stack(TSParser *self) {
   bool made_changes = false;
   unsigned min_error_cost = UINT_MAX;
@@ -2492,6 +2517,16 @@
           break;
         }
       }
+
+      // The version completed its turn. A merge with a version before it stops the list from
+      // growing past the mid-step limit of `ts_parser__reduce`. The list is already longer than the
+      // condense step at the end of the loop keeps.
+      if (
+        ts_stack_version_count(self->stack) > MAX_VERSION_COUNT &&
+        ts_parser__merge_finished_version(self, version)
+      ) {
+        version--;
+      }
     }
 
     // After advancing each version of the stack, re-sort the versions by their cost,
